## Partition Variables

Let:

```java
Deque<Integer> countStack = new ArrayDeque<>();
Deque<StringBuilder> stringStack = new ArrayDeque<>();
StringBuilder currStr = new StringBuilder();
int currK = 0;
```

---

### Border Elements

Using `StringBuilder` stacks instead of standard `String` objects completely avoids unnecessary string reference generations during stack transitions:

```java
stringStack.push(currStr);
currStr = new StringBuilder(); // Reset to clear scope safely
```

---

## Correct Partition Condition

The repetition reconstruction loop decodes text blocks inside a single synchronized step upon striking a closing token:

```java
int repeatTimes = countStack.pop();
StringBuilder decodedSegment = stringStack.pop();
while (repeatTimes > 0) {
    decodedSegment.append(currStr);
    repeatTimes--;
}
currStr = decodedSegment;
```

